#!/usr/bin/python3 -B
"""aurum-ws - Aurum Workstation v1 (SPEC lab/workstation/SPEC.md v0.7). Local AI on your existing Ubuntu, with undo.

  sudo aurum-ws plan     [--privacy] [--theme] [--model TAG]   show what install would do (changes nothing)
  sudo aurum-ws install  [--privacy] [--theme] [--model TAG]   do it (resumes an interrupted install)
  sudo aurum-ws status                                        every step + a test answer + GPU line
  sudo aurum-ws undo     [--purge-models] [--force]           remove what Aurum created (README: what is kept)

Safety rules (SPEC): runs only as root from the root-owned stage; an existing Ollama is ADOPTED = only read, never
changed (no pulls into it); installs no apt packages and no drivers; Ollama listens on 127.0.0.1 only; every change is
recorded (with its pre-state) in /var/lib/aurum-ws/manifest.json BEFORE it is made, and an interrupted step is
inspected (pre-state / intended state / something else -> stop) before anything is redone or undone; root never
follows a path a user controls (user-scoped steps run AS that user).
"""
